WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.260
The heroes and villains of the Marvel Cinematic
Universe got snap-happy in Avengers: Endgame,

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:10.470
and one click of the fingers created a potential
problem for a much-loved character: Zoe Saldana's

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:11.020
Gamora.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:16.080
Avengers: Endgame directors Joe and Anthony
Russo have addressed the green-skinned heroine's

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.780
fate, but their answer isn't as crystal-clear
as most fans might hope.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.980
After Avengers: Endgame leaps forward five
years to the year 2023 following the fallout

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:29.660
of Avengers: Infinity War, the surviving heroes
concoct a plan to travel back in time, collect

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.320
the Infinity Stones ahead of when Thanos took
them, then jump to the present to equip their

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.690
own Infinity Gauntlet and resurrect their
fallen compatriots.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:38.840
"Time travel!"

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.650
The time heist is successful, despite a number
of hiccups along the way, and the heroes who

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:47.960
were dusted in Infinity War came back to life
to fight a final battle against Thanos.

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:52.860
But those characters weren't the only ones
who returned to the MCU in Endgame: Gamora

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:58.489
did, too - but as the 2014 version of herself
prior to Guardians of the Galaxy and prior

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:00.160
to her death in Infinity War.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:05.190
She showed up in 2023 after Professor Hulk
used his Infinity Gauntlet to bring back the

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:10.340
dusted heroes, and before Tony Stark snapped
his fingers to decimate Thanos and his army.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:16.330
This raised a pressing question: If 2018 Gamora
was killed when Thanos sacrificed her to obtain

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:21.600
the Soul Stone in Infinity War, what happened
to 2014 Gamora after Tony's snap?

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:26.480
Chatting with Business Insider's Travis Clark,
the Russos said that there's an equal chance

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:31.890
that 2014 Gamora was spared in Tony's snap
as there is the possibility she died alongside

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.380
Thanos and his supporters.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.510
Additionally, Marvel fans will likely have
to wait until Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:41.870
3 hits theaters sometime in the future to
learn what really happened to Gamora after

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:42.780
Tony's snap.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:47.220
Shutting down any speculation about whether
Gamora's fellow Guardians know the answer,

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.000
Anthony Russo added that Star-Lord is just
as in the dark as fans are.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:55.340
Joe Russo then noted that he's confident "future
films will answer that question."

00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:00.160
When Clark commented that it's up to Guardians
Vol. 3 director James Gunn to fully unravel

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.580
the mystery, Anthony agreed, saying, quote,
"Exactly, we've done our job."

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.840
It's not all that implausible to think that
2014 Gamora may have survived the climactic

00:02:09.849 --> 00:02:14.870
battle between Thanos and the Avengers, despite
her seemingly being considered a part of Thanos'

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:18.540
intergalactic army and not appearing in physical
form after Tony's snap.

00:02:19.049 --> 00:02:22.920
She does, however, show up on a screen map
in the Guardians' ship the Benatar at the

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.680
end of the film.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.230
It seems evident that Star-Lord and the rest
of the team will embark on a mission to locate

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.800
Gamora in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:35.300
Considering how pivotal to the franchise Gamora
has been, it's only right that she would emerge

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.000
once more for the trilogy-ender.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:42.419
If and when Gamora returns in the third Guardians
film, it's basically guaranteed that the heroine

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.420
will be the 2014 Gamora who flashed forward
in time in Endgame.

00:02:46.769 --> 00:02:50.440
The Gamora who played a part in the first
two Guardians movies and Avengers: Infinity

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.900
War is dead and cannot be revived.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.000
As Endgame co-writer Christopher Markus once
explained,

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.880
"When Gamora went off that cliff [in Infinity
War] the Gamora from that time period died."

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:06.000
Joe Russo confirmed elsewhere when speaking
about Black Widow's death that non-snap deaths

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:07.010
are permanent.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:07.540
He said:

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.480
"[The] process is irreversible.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:13.180
Even if you have returned [the Soul Stone]
to its original location, you wouldn't be

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:14.560
able to get the person back.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:19.020
In fact, it's not really returning the stone,
more like put it back properly.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:23.690
The tribute soul for the Soul Stone will forever
be sealed in that place, therefore Black Widow

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:24.980
is gone forever."

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:31.260
If Black Widow and Gamora experienced the
same demise, that means 2018 Gamora is gone

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:31.940
forever as well.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.020
Past Gamora may not be, though.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.340
And even if she was dusted when Tony snapped
his fingers, there's a chance she could return

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.020
to life in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3.

